<title>USA: Sri Lanka buys 100,000 T wheat - trade.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka buys 100,000 T wheat - trade.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka overnight bought a total of 100,000 tonnes of wheat for late October-November shipment, U.S. exporters said.  </p>
<p>The wheat was divided into two lots of 50,000 tonnes each. One 50,000-tonne-lot purchased was comprised of U.S. soft white wheat for October 28-November 6 delivery, they said.</p>
<p>Another 50,000 tonnes was Australian hard wheat for November 11-20 shipment, a U.S. exporter said.</p>
<p>Prices were not given and no other details were available.</p>
<p>--Doris Frankel 312-983-7305</p>
</text>
